# Forever Party Rentals — 301 redirects from old Squarespace URLs to new static site
# Format: OLD_PATH  NEW_PATH  STATUS
# Works on Netlify and Cloudflare Pages (drop this file at site root).
# First match wins — keep specific paths above any catch-alls.
#
# CANONICAL URL FORM: extensionless (e.g. /burnaby-party-rentals, /chairs).
# Netlify pretty_urls = true (set in netlify.toml) serves `foo.html` at /foo
# and 301-redirects /foo.html → /foo automatically — no rules needed here.

# ── Static assets that MUST serve as-is (top of file, before catch-alls) ────
# Netlify's `:slug` placeholder matches dotted filenames like `shared.css`.
# These explicit 200! rules pin them at their canonical path.
/shared.css                                                             /shared.css                                                     200!
/shared.js                                                              /shared.js                                                      200!
/sitemap.xml                                                            /sitemap.xml                                                    200!
/robots.txt                                                             /robots.txt                                                     200!
/llms.txt                                                               /llms.txt                                                       200!
/favicon.svg                                                            /favicon.svg                                                    200!
/favicon.ico                                                            /favicon.ico                                                    200!
/_headers                                                               /_headers                                                       200!

# ── Planner short share links (/p/<id>) ─────────────────────────────────────
# 200 rewrite (NOT a redirect): the hub page is served at the short URL and
# its inline boot script resolves <id> via GET /api/share/<id>, then
# history.replaceState()s to /event-layout-planner#s=<payload> before the
# planner iframe loads. Target keeps the .html extension — rewrite targets
# must name the real file in the publish dir (pretty_urls only rewrites
# inbound request URLs, not rule targets). /api/share itself needs no rule:
# Functions v2 routes declare their own path (see netlify/functions/share.mjs).
/p/*                                                                    /event-layout-planner.html                                      200
/home                                                                   /                                                               301!
/about-us                                                               /                                                               301

